---
// The privacy page's text in English. Its layout and styles are in
// src/pages/[lang]/privacy.astro; every language needs its own file here.
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from "astro:i18n";
import { sharePaths } from "../../../data/nav";
import { contactEmail, owner } from "../../../data/site";

interface Props {
  lang: string;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="updated">Last updated: 3 October 2026</p>

<p class="lead">
  Handball Coachboard sets no cookies and has no accounts. Your drawing stays on your device until
  you share it.
</p>

<h2>Who runs this site</h2>
<p>
  Handball Coachboard is run by {owner}. Questions about your privacy? Email <a
    href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a
  >. We only use your address and your message to reply to you.
</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>
  This site sets no cookies, first-party or third-party. There are no ads either. The statistics
  below work without cookies. That's why there is no cookie banner.
</p>

<h2>The board</h2>
<p>
  The board keeps your drawing in your browser's storage, on your own device. That way it's still
  there next time. It only leaves your device when you share it.
</p>
<p>
  In a shared link, the drawing sits after the <code>#</code> in the address. Your browser doesn't
  send that part to any server. That means we don't see what you draw. Your browser also makes the
  QR code itself.
</p>

<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>
  The site runs on Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site against abuse, Cloudflare
  processes technical data, such as your IP address and your browser. Every web server does that.
  We don't use that data to identify you. See the <a
    href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
    rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a
  >.
</p>

<h2>Statistics</h2>
<p>
  The board pages load <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener"
    >Cloudflare Web Analytics</a
  >. That tells us whether coaches use the board, and how fast it is on their phones. The other
  pages load no script at all.
</p>
<p>
  Web Analytics counts page views and measures loading speed. It works without cookies, without
  storage in your browser and without fingerprinting. Cloudflare receives:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    the address of the page, without the part after the <code>#</code> or <code>?</code>, so not
    your drawing either;
  </li>
  <li>the page you came from;</li>
  <li>your browser, operating system and device type;</li>
  <li>your country;</li>
  <li>how fast the page loaded and responded.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Cloudflare drops your IP address at its nearest data center and doesn't store it. Cloudflare
  keeps the statistics for six months.
</p>
<p>
  A shared link opens <code>{getRelativeLocaleUrl(lang, sharePaths.link)}</code>, a QR
  code <code>{getRelativeLocaleUrl(lang, sharePaths.qr)}</code>. That shows us how often shared
  boards are opened. We don't see what's on them.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>When something changes, we update this page and the date at the top.</p>
